## Provider interface

The page defines the contract as `ApiPlatform\State\ProviderInterface`, which custom providers implement:

```php
public function provide(Operation $operation, array $uriVariables = [], array $context = []): iterable|BlogPost|null
```

The return type in the examples varies. Single-item providers return the object or `null`, and collection providers return an iterable. The page's docblock examples use `@implements ProviderInterface<...>` for generics.

## Collections

The page shows a collection provider returning a plain array (`$this->data`) when the operation is a `CollectionOperationInterface`. It does not mention `TraversablePaginator` or any other paginator class.

## Operation, URI variables, and context

- **`$operation`**: the `Operation` instance. The examples use `instanceof CollectionOperationInterface` to distinguish collection from item requests.
- **`$uriVariables`**: an array of URI variable values, such as `$uriVariables['id']`.
- **`$context`**: the page does not describe its contents.
- **Filters and request**: the page does not cover how to access them.

## Errors

The page does not name any HTTP exception classes. It documents one behavior: "API Platform will automatically generate a 404 response if the provider returns `null`." The only exceptions it names are `RuntimeException`s thrown for invalid `repositoryMethod` configuration, which are not HTTP errors.

## Example: custom provider on a plain resource class

```php
<?php
// src/ApiResource/BlogPost.php
namespace App\ApiResource;

use ApiPlatform\Metadata\ApiProperty;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\ApiResource;
use App\State\BlogPostProvider;

#[ApiResource(provider: BlogPostProvider::class)]
class BlogPost
{
    #[ApiProperty(identifier: true)]
    public string $id;

    public string $title;
}
```

```php
<?php
// src/State/BlogPostProvider.php
namespace App\State;

use ApiPlatform\Metadata\CollectionOperationInterface;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\Operation;
use ApiPlatform\State\ProviderInterface;
use App\ApiResource\BlogPost;

/**
 * @implements ProviderInterface<BlogPost[]|BlogPost|null>
 */
final class BlogPostProvider implements ProviderInterface
{
    private array $data;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $ab = new BlogPost();
        $ab->id = 'ab';
        $ab->title = 'First post';

        $this->data = ['ab' => $ab];
    }

    public function provide(Operation $operation, array $uriVariables = [], array $context = []): iterable|BlogPost|null
    {
        if ($operation instanceof CollectionOperationInterface) {
            return array_values($this->data);
        }

        return $this->data[$uriVariables['id']] ?? null;
    }
}
```

